{#
  The parameter section of a function or method.

  Rendered only where at least one parameter carries a doc comment, since a
  table of empty cells says less than the signature already did. Every
  parameter appears once it renders: the signature is abbreviated in that case,
  so the table is the only place the full list is written.

  The Type column is filled from a parenthesised type opening the description,
  which is a stopgap until the language carries type annotations of its own.
#}
{#
  A function/method's `<code>signature -> ReturnType</code>` heading, with
  the arrow and type appended inside the same `<code>` element when its doc
  comment opened with a parenthesised type (see _split_type in __init__.py)
  -- the arrow form anticipates the language's own eventual return-type
  syntax, so it belongs inside `<code>` as prospective real syntax rather
  than as descriptive text tacked on after it.

  The return type is run through `convert_markdown` (real links, same as a
  parameter's Type column) rather than left as plain text inside `sig`,
  since `heading()`'s content is inserted as literal HTML, not reprocessed
  as Markdown itself. Building `content` has to go through a `{% set %}
  ... {% endset %}` capture block, which uses Jinja's own output-escaping
  pipeline to combine the literal text and `convert_markdown`'s `Markup`
  result -- joining them with a plain `~` expression instead reaches
  Python's own operator dispatch, where `Markup.__radd__`/`__add__` treat
  themselves as the one safe operand and auto-escape everything *else* in
  the expression, corrupting the literal `<code>` tags too.
#}
{% macro signature_heading(sig, return_type, heading_level, id, role, toc_label) %}
{% set content %}<code>{{ sig }}{% if return_type %} -&gt; {{ return_type | convert_markdown(heading_level, id ~ "--returns", strip_paragraph=true) }}{% endif %}</code>{% endset %}
{{ content | trim | heading(heading_level, role=role, id=id, toc_label=toc_label) }}
{% endmacro %}

{% macro parameters(entity, heading_level, base_id) %}
{% if entity.params | selectattr("documented") | list %}
{{ "Parameters" | heading(heading_level, skip_inventory=true, id=base_id ~ "--parameters") }}
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for p in entity.params %}
<tr>
  <td><code>{{ p.name }}{{ "?" if p.optional }}</code></td>
  <td>{% if p.type %}{{ p.type | convert_markdown(heading_level, base_id ~ "--" ~ p.slug, strip_paragraph=true) }}{% endif %}</td>
  <td>{{ p.doc_short | convert_markdown(heading_level, base_id ~ "--" ~ p.slug, strip_paragraph=true) }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{#
  A parameter documented past its first paragraph gets a subsection of its own,
  so the table keeps one line per parameter however much there is to say.
#}
{% for p in entity.params if p.doc_rest %}
{% set param_id = base_id ~ "--" ~ p.slug %}
{{ ("<code>" ~ p.name ~ "</code>") | heading(heading_level + 1, skip_inventory=true, id=param_id, toc_label=p.name) }}
{{ p.doc_rest | convert_markdown(heading_level + 2, param_id) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
